window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-048", "name_zh": "完形", "name_en": "gestalt", "tagline": "赛斯借来的一个词（gestalt）：部分组成的整体会大于总和——你的身体、人格、一个家庭、一块岩石乃至整个宇宙，都是意识一层层「完形」出来的，而每一部分在整体里都不丢失自己。", "explanation": "「完形」（gestalt，也译完型）是赛斯从心理学借来的词，却是他整套宇宙观的主要脚手架：部分组成的整体大于总和，而部分并不因此消失。它的第一性质是「融合而不吞并」——合成完形时个体性不减反增。赛斯用它解释一切：你的潜意识是肉体每个原子分子合作维持的完形；自我是分子意识聚成的完形意识在强度巅峰时升起的结果；连玻璃杯、岩石、地球都是各自层次的完形；你们的宇宙本身就是一整个完形。往上，佛陀与「上帝」被他重新描述为心灵完形、能量完形，早期课里他更喜欢称之为原始能量完形；晚年的创世故事里，一切万有是那个所有存在由之而出的神圣心理完形，意识单位在其中开始创造时空。往下，家庭、团体、一堂课都各自是活的完形，有自己的主观身份。对个人最实用的推论是：人格这个精神完形靠行动的自由流动维持效率，疾病不是它的一部分，而创造——包括一幅画——本身就是新完形的诞生。意识的算术是乘法不是除法：完形越滚越大，而每个身份始终记得它与整体的联盟。", "definitions": [{"zh": "心灵是有知觉的能量的统一完型（gestalt），在其中住着你不可侵犯的本体，当你实现你的潜能时，它却一直在变。", "en": "The psyche is a gestalt of aware energy in which your own identity resides, inviolate, yet ever-changing as you fulfill your potentials.", "source": "Session 758"}, {"zh": "我们说，一个意识就是感知模式的一个完形，行动藉此认识它自己。", "en": "We therefore say that a consciousness is a gestalt of patterns of perception, by which action knows itself.", "source": "Session 141"}, {"zh": "你们从这一点应该看到，你们的宇宙本身因此就是一个完形。", "en": "Now, you should see from this that your universe is therefore itself a gestalt.", "source": "Session 57"}, {"zh": "我们所会有的是一个完形，你们的个体性不会减少一分一毫，而是一种带来更大能力的融合。", "en": "What we will have when this happens is a gestalt, with no lessening of your individualities at all, but a merging that will bring greater abilities.", "source": "Session 27"}, {"zh": "因此你们站在一个恒常的盎然生机之中，站在一个有知觉的能量完形之中。", "en": "So you stand amid a constant vital commotion, a gestalt of aware energy", "source": "Session 512"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "「完形」是什么意思？", "note": "AI总结：完形是赛斯书里描述意识如何组织的关键词，指部分聚成的整体大于总和、却又不像团队那样挤掉个人。它最基本的性质在第 27 节那句话里就说清了：融合成一个完形时，你的个体性不会减少一分一毫，反而带来更大的能力。顺着这条线，赛斯给了一系列定义：一个意识就是感知模式的完形，行动借此认识自己；一个自己也是行动的完形，由它不同的层面以不同方式感知；许多层面组成全我，许多自己又形成一个你知之甚少的更大完形——而自己们的完形绝不暗含放弃个人性。往大处说，心理架构和心灵完形构成一切系统里个别实相的基础，「整体」之所以有意义，正因为它透过自觉的个别部分意识它自己。心灵本身就是有知觉的能量的统一完型，你的本体住在里面，不可侵犯却一直在变；也可以把一个自己想作意识之能量完形的核心。要紧的是完形不是静定的成品：它们永远在变为中，不断结盟，不是封闭的单位。", "src": "第 27、141、215、218、233、306、680、725、744、758、787 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 27 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 141 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 215 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 218 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 233 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 306 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 680 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 725 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 744 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 758 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 787 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-048-e0001", "zh": "现在我不能更进一步谈这件事，因为我还没有给你们相关的原则。一旦发生这个状况，我们就会有一个完形，你们的个体性不会减少一分一毫，而是一种带来更大能力的融合。", "en": "I cannot go further into this now because I have not given you the principles involved as yet. What we will have when this happens is a gestalt, with no lessening of your individualities at all, but a merging that will bring greater abilities.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第27节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "27", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0092", "zh": "一个特定的意识是这些观念模式的一个完形；但什么都阻止不了意识透过经验其他观念模式或感知模式来提升它自己。这种吸收会增长，而不是削减任何既定的意识。我们使用，或你们使用，语言文字只不过是为了方便而已。所以我们说，一个意识就是感知模式的一个完形，行动藉此认识它自己。但是感知模式可能会成长，意识也会往外伸展。意识已经改变了。它不再是相同的意识，因为它已经扩展自己。可是另一方面，它也是同样的意识，因为它就是已经扩展的那个意识。所以，语言文字可能让我们一头雾水。", "en": "A particular consciousness is a gestalt of these conceptual patterns; but there is nothing to prevent a consciousness from increasing itself by experiencing other conceptual patterns or patterns of perception. This assimilation would increase, not decrease, any given consciousness. We use, or you use, words merely as a convenience. We therefore say that a consciousness is a gestalt of patterns of perception, by which action knows itself. But the patterns of perceptions may grow, and the consciousness reach out. The consciousness has changed. It is no longer the same consciousness, since it has extended itself. Yet it is the same consciousness, on the other hand, because it is that which has extended itself. So words can confuse us.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第141节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "141", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0095", "zh": "不过，如果我们改变我们任意断定的界限点，那么较小的自己这时不管在哪一头似乎都是其他的自己所属的各个部分。为了实际的目的，可以说一个自己组成一个感知模式完形，在那些模式之内维持着一种相当持续的效率。这时候我可以给你们的定义，最贴切的就是这一个了。", "en": "If however we changed our arbitrary boundary points, then the minor selves at either end would now seem to be portions of other selves. For practical purposes it may be said that a self is composed of a gestalt of perception patterns, within which a fairly constant efficiency is maintained. This is the best definition I can give you at this time.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第141节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "141", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0130", "zh": "自我试图把行动分解为更小的单位。直觉试着感知行动的整体。自我是为了检验的目的而分解，而直觉是组成。自我和直觉都在执行它们的功能，很明显地创造了行动。自己当然可能以一种行动的完形来考虑，由它自己不同的层面以不同的方式来感知。", "en": "The ego attempts to break down action into smaller and smaller units. The intuitions try to perceive action as a whole. The ego breaks down for purposes of examination, the intuitions construct. Both the ego and the intuitions, in performing their functions, obviously create action. The self may of course be considered as a gestalt of action, perceived in a different manner by various levels of itself.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第215节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "215", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0132", "zh": "我不认为唐尼了解这个。在某一点过后，并没有他想像中的连载，单纯是因为透过一连串不同时间的自己们的这种发展不再是必要的。自己们会达到一个点，那不是一个理论上的点，而是一个特别的数学上存在的点，借此，这些时间和自己们简单地变成了一个——用我们的字眼——存有。 我必须强调，个人性是永远不会失去的。但这个主题太复杂，今晚无法涵盖。不过我们在谈到行动的时候曾经解释过，自己们的完形并不暗含着放弃个人性。这里要记得，转世是一个简单的事实，但它却不被普莱斯利或唐尼所接受。", "en": "I do not believe that Dunne understood this. There is no serialization as he imagined, after a certain point, simply because this progression of selves through various times in a serial fashion is no longer necessary. The selves reach a point which is not a theoretical point, but a particular mathematically existent point, whereby these times and selves simply become one, or in our terms, an entity. I must stress that individuality is never lost. But this is too complicated a subject to cover this evening. We have explained it rather adequately in terms of action however, and gestalts of selves do not imply a giving-up of individuality at all. It should be remembered here that reincarnation is simply a fact, and one which is not accepted by Priestley or Dunne.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第218节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "218", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0137", "zh": "因为自己的很多层面组成了全我，所以很多的自己形成了一个你们所知甚少的完形，这我还没准备要告诉你们。", "en": "For as many layers of the self compose the whole self, so many selves form a gestalt of which you know relatively little, and of which I am not yet prepared to tell you.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第233节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "233", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0165", "zh": "这并不是说这个词事实上没有意义。心理架构和心灵完形构成个别实相的基础，不论是什么系统。这些全都隐含一个整体，但是再一次，整体这个词是没有意义的，如果整体，透过自觉的个别部分，对它自己没有意识的话。", "en": "This does not mean that the word indeed would have no meaning. Psychological frameworks and psychic gestalts form the basis for individual reality regardless of system. All of these do imply a whole, but the very term whole would again be meaningless if the whole, through self conscious individual parts, were not conscious of itself.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第306节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "306", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0232", "zh": "意识是由能量组成的，因此，能量所暗示的一切也都包含在意识里。那么，心灵可以被想作是能量之高度充电的“粒子”之聚合物，遵循着某些法则与属性，而其中有许多是你们根本不知道的。在其他的层面上，动力学的律则可适用于“自己”之能量来源。将一个“自己”想作是一个意识之能量完形的核心。那个核心按照其强度将会吸引来那个本体所能有的整个能量模式之某些团块。", "en": "Consciousness is composed of energy, with everything that implies. The psyche, then, can be thought of as a conglomeration of highly charged “particles” of energy, following rules and properties, many simply unknown to you. On other levels, laws of dynamics apply to the energy sources of the self. Think of a given “self” as a nucleus of an energy gestalt of consciousness. That nucleus, according to its intensity, will attract to it certain masses of the entire energy patterns available to a given identity.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第680节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "680", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0245", "zh": "以同样的方式，十分分开的身份可以在一个相互取予的完形里与其它的身份混合，在其中，整体的意图就如这桌子的形状一样清楚。到某个程度，约瑟感知到那种内在的心灵组织。", "en": "In the same way, quite separate identities can merge with others in a give-and-take gestalt, in which the overall intent is as clear as the shape of the table. To some extent Joseph was perceiving that kind of inner psychic organization.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第725节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "725", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0251", "zh": "当心灵完形被形成时，它们并非静定的。它们形成不同的联盟，直到它们在一个整个的本体里找到适合它们目的的位置，或强大到能变得不可毁灭。它们永远在变为（Becoming）中，它们并不是封闭的单位。", "en": "When psychic gestalts are formed they are not static. They make different alliances until they find their place in a whole identity that serves their purposes, or are strong enough to become indestructible. They are always becoming. They are not closed units.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0258", "zh": "心灵是有知觉的能量的统一完型（gestalt），在其中住着你不可侵犯的本体，当你实现你的潜能时，它却一直在变。", "en": "(Long pause at 10:33.) The psyche is a gestalt of aware energy in which your own identity resides, inviolate, yet ever-changing as you fulfill your potentials.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第758节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "758", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0260", "zh": "基本上，心灵是纯粹能量在一种特殊形式的表象（manifestation）。在你所熟知的架构之外考虑心灵经验，是颇为困难的。你要求定义与术语的某种精确性。当然，那词汇自动地结构了讯息。 心灵是能量完形（energy gestalt）的一个聚集物（conglomeration）。要了解那个，你必须悟到纯粹能量有这种改变「模式形成」（pattern forming）的倾向，以致它总是以表象出现。它变成心灵的「伪装」（camouflage）。", "en": "Basically, the psyche is a manifestation of pure energy in a particular form. It is very difficult to consider its experience outside of the framework familiar to you. You demand a certain preciseness of definition and terminology. That vocabulary automatically structures the information, of course. The psyche is a conglomeration of energy gestalts. To understand that, you must realize that pure energy has such transforming pattern-forming propensities that it always appears as its manifestations. It becomes its “camouflages.”", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第787节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "787", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "为什么说万物都是完形？——从细胞到整个宇宙", "note": "AI总结：完形不是玄谈，赛斯用它解释了「东西」是怎么来的。你的潜意识就不是一个躲在脑壳里的局部机构，而是由肉体每一个原子与分子的合作意识维持形成的完形；结合起来的分子意识保住本体、形成完形意识，那就是自我。往上数也一样：细胞和分子把心灵完形转化为人体这样一个独立结构；连一只玻璃杯，都是有自己浓缩理解的分子原子一起形成的「玻璃杯完形」；岩石由各有意识的原子分子形成岩石的完形意识；树木、岩石、你的身体组织都分享着完形意识。更惊人的推论有两条：一，你的自我看似单一，其实是集体意识的结果，它依赖住在你每个活细胞里的微细意识；二，你们的宇宙本身因此就是一个完形——就像一个细胞可以被视为与身体其余部分分离，自己也可以被视为与宇宙分离，但那道边界只是画出来的。所谓「对自己的意识」，就是当身体各层完形意识达到某种强度巅峰时升起的东西。", "src": "第 51、55、57、66、87、505、512、568、613、654、664、705 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 51 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 55 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 57 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 66 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 87 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 505 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 512 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 568 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 613 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 654 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 664 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 705 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-048-e0008", "zh": "这种物质宇宙的持续创造，不是通过存在于两耳之间、额头后方某个局部的潜意识来维持的。个体的潜意识，我解释过，是心灵资源与能力之池的成果。它是一个完形，由构成肉体的每一个原子与分子合作、整体的意识维持和形成。", "en": "Now, this constant creation of the physical universe is not maintained through some localized subconscious that exists somewhere between two ears, behind the forehead. The individual subconscious, as I have explained, is the result of a psychic pooling of resources and abilities. It is a gestalt, maintained and formed by the cooperating, generalized consciousness of each atom and molecule of which the physical body is composed.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第51节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "51", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0012", "zh": "把它们的心灵完形转化为一个特定人类物质结构的细胞与分子，是从你们可称为外在环境之处分离出来的，但是它们与外在环境的连结程度却大过它们与外在环境的分离程度。是内在自我、内在生命力以及内在自我的决心，在构成肉体的所有细胞合作之下，才让人体这样一个特定的结构能够以分离的独立建构状态存在，并维持必要的本体感。", "en": "The cells and molecules, forming their psychic gestalt into a particular human physical structure, are separated from what you might call the outer environment, and yet they are also connected to the outer environment more than they are separated from it. It is the inner ego, and the inner vitality and the inner ego’s determination, along with the cooperation of all the cells that compose the physical body, that enables such a particular structure as the human body to exist as a separate construction, and to maintain the necessary sense of identity.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0015", "zh": "这结合的分子意识，保留本体，形成一个完形意识，就是自我、外在自我，接着再被内在自我的意识利用。内在自我不受你们层面的法则牵制，只要它在物质的诞生时进入你们的层面，就能离开肉体，再重建它。", "en": "The combined molecular consciousnesses, retaining identity, form a gestalt consciousness that is the ego, the outer ego, that is in turn utilized by the consciousness of the inner ego. The inner ego being unhampered by the laws of your plane, once having entered your plane at physical birth, can therefore leave the physical body and then reconstruct it.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0022", "zh": "你们从这一点应该看到，你们的宇宙本身因此就是一个完形。当一个细胞可以被认为是与身体其余部分分离的，当它的外缘可以被认为是隔开它与身体其余部分的，那么自己就可以被认为是与宇宙分离的，而它的外皮也可以被想成是隔开它与身体的其他部分。", "en": "Now, you should see from this that your universe is therefore itself a gestalt. As an individual cell can be considered to be apart from the rest of the body, as its outer rim can be considered as something that divides it from the rest of the body, so the self can be considered as apart from the universe, and its outer skin thought of as dividing it from the rest of the body.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第57节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "57", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0040", "zh": "每一个玻璃杯都是由非常真实的分子和原子建构的，每一个分子与原子都有它们自己的整体意识与浓缩理解，一起形成称为玻璃杯的完形。", "en": "Each physical glass is constructed of quite real molecules and atoms, which have their own generalized consciousness and capsule comprehension, and which form together in the gestalt called a glass.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第66节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "66", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0054", "zh": "这一点极为重要。因此，不管是像人类或动物那种复杂的心灵完形，还是像一颗细胞或分子那样比较简单的完形，两者所属的意识无论如何全部都在其中运作，并且在它们四周形成精神或心灵围场，在围场之内自然包含浓缩理解，这是所有能量都具有的一个特性。", "en": "This point is extremely important. All consciousness, therefore, either of a complicated psychic gestalt such as a man or animal, or of simpler gestalts such as an individual cell or molecule, nevertheless operate in and form about themselves mental or psychic enclosures, within which is naturally contained the capsule comprehension which is an attribute of all energy.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第87节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "87", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0202", "zh": "这些单位——让我们来谈谈它们，比如说，同一块岩石的关系。岩石由原子与分子构成，各有各的意识。这就形成了岩石的完形意识。", "en": "These units—let us discuss them as they are related, for example, to a rock. The rock is composed of atoms and molecules each with their own consciousness. This forms a gestalt-rock-consciousness.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第505节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "505", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0206", "zh": "无论如何，在钉子内的原子与分子确实拥有它们自己的一种意识。组成这书页的原子与分子在它们自己的层面内也有知觉。没有一样存在的东西——不管是石头、矿物、植物、动物或空气——不是充满了它自己的那种意识的。因此你们站在一个恒常的盎然生机之中，站在一个有知觉的能量完形之中，而你们自己的肉体也是由有意识的细胞所组成，它们在自己内带着对自己身份的体认，它们甘愿合作以形成一个有形的结构，那就是你们的肉体。", "en": "Nevertheless, the atoms and molecules within the nail do possess their own kind of consciousness. The atoms and molecules that make up the pages of this book are also, within their own level, aware. Nothing exists — neither rock, mineral, plant, animal, or air — that is not filled with consciousness of its own kind. So you stand amid a constant vital commotion, a gestalt of aware energy, and you are yourselves physically composed of conscious cells that carry within themselves the realization of their own identity, that cooperate willingly to form the corporeal structure that is your physical body.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "512", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0215", "zh": "许多可能系统的感知机制和你们的大不相同。事实上，有些是建立在你们完全陌生的知觉完形上。举例来说，你并没有了解到你的“自我”是集体意识的结果。那个最直接面对外在世界的意识，是依赖着居住于你身体的每一个活细胞内的微细意识，而一般言之你只觉知到一个自我——至少在某一时刻。", "en": "Many probable systems have perceptive mechanisms far different from your own. In fact, some are based upon gestalts of awareness completely alien to you. Quite without realizing it, your ego is a result of group consciousness, for example; the one consciousness that most directly faces the exterior world, is dependent upon the minute consciousness that resides within each living cell of your body; and as a rule you are only aware of one ego — at least at a time.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第568节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "568", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0223", "zh": "树木、岩石都有自己的意识，并且，它们分享着一个“完形意识”（gestalt consciousness） 就如你自己身体中有生命的组织，也是一样。（译注：gestalt，心理学名词，意指一个整体的、不可分的结构或模式，具有明确的特性，同时带有一种整体的经验。既不能以整体中的部分来划分，亦不能简单地归纳成一种个别小单位聚集而成的总和。简单而言就是一种“形态场”。）细胞与器官也全都有其自己的意识，以及一种完形意识。因此，“人类”除了个人有个别的意识之外，也一样有着一种完整的或集体的意识，只不过就个人而言，这种意识几乎根本就察觉不到罢了。", "en": "Trees and rocks possess their own consciousness, and also share a gestalt consciousness, even as the living portions of your body. The cells and organs have their own awarenesses, and a gestalt one. So the race of man also has individual consciousness and a gestalt or mass consciousness, of which you individually are hardly aware.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第613节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "613", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0228", "zh": "现在：纯就身体而言，当组成肉体的原子、分子、细胞与器官的完形意识达到某种强度巅峰时，你们认为的“对自己的意识”便从中升起。", "en": "Now: In purely physical terms, what you think of as consciousness of the self arises from a certain peak of intensity reached by the gestalt consciousness of the atoms and molecules, and cells and organs, that compose the body.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第654节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "654", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0230", "zh": "你身体和意识的节奏遵循着你们行星的模式。然而，这行星本身是由原子与分子组成的，每一个原子与分子都有其自己那类的意识，实质结构就由它们的“完形”与累积的合作组织——由意识——形成。", "en": "The rhythms of your body and of your consciousness follow the patterns of your planet. The planet itself is composed of atoms and molecules, each with their own kind of consciousness, however; and in the gestalt and cumulative cooperative organization of their nature the physical structure is formed — out of consciousness.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第664节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "664", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0244", "zh": "所有这些呈现出一幅十分错误的画面。实质地说，地球本身有它自己那种的完形意识。如果你一定要的话，那么你可以把地球意识想作是由相当“迟钝的”沙尘及石子向着矿物、植物及动物王国按等级上升的一个大的觉性斜坡（slope of awareness）。即使如此，要记住，那些王国其实并没有这样分隔开，而是每一个都和其它的非常密切的相连。在一个这种王国发生的任何事，没有不影响到其它的王国的，不过，在那些仿佛分离的系统之间存在着一个了不起的天生合作。如果你记得，甚至原子与分子也有意识，那么，你就比较容易了解，的确有某一种的觉性统合着这些王国。", "en": "All of this presented a quite erroneous picture. Physically speaking, earth itself has its own kind of gestalt consciousness. If you must, then think of that earth consciousness as grading (spelled) upward in great slopes of awareness from relatively “inert” particles of dust and stone through the mineral, vegetable, and animal kingdoms. Even then, remember that those kingdoms are not so separate after all. Each one is highly related to each of the others. Nothing happens in one such kingdom that does not affect the others. A great, gracious cooperation exists between those seemingly separate systems, however. If you will remember that even atoms and molecules have consciousness, then it will be easier for you to understand that there is indeed a certain kind of awareness that unites these kingdoms.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第705节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "705", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "最大的那些完形：上帝、金字塔与神圣完形", "note": "AI总结：赛斯讲「神」时用的主要工具就是完形。他说佛陀在你们的说法里不是一个个人，而是一个心灵完形、能量完形；如果你要把那个至高无上、绝对的心灵完形叫作上帝，那就别想把他物质化——他是你细胞的核，比呼吸与你更亲密。早期课里他给过一个更合用的词：原始能量完形——那些金字塔能量完形既取得统一的特质和高度的智力，形成的又只是人类上帝观的近似；人们信仰里的形象至多代表它被扭曲的一小面。这些「心灵完形金字塔」代表所有开始与所有结束，又扩展成新的开始；它们的价值完成经验远超任何人类，却又关心你们之中最小的存在；基督的传奇在某种意义上正是人类对这类金字塔完形的内在认可。到晚年讲创世时，这个思路收拢成「神圣的心理完形」：它是所有存在由之而出的来源，一切万有作为原初的意识完形渴望进一步的存在，意识单位就在这个神圣完形之内开始创造时间、空间和你们的宇宙。", "src": "第 81、95、96、177、203、213、297、311、426、886、888、889 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 81 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 95 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 96 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 177 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 203 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 213 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 297 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 311 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 426 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 886 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 888 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 889 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-048-e0047", "zh": "他并不是你们所说的人类，但他经历过人的阶段；佛教的神话最接近这个类似的实相。以你们的话来说，他不是一个人，而是一个心灵完形，一个能量完形。", "en": "He is not human in your terms, though he passed through human stages; and here the Buddhist's myth comes closest to approximating reality. He is not one individual, in your terms, but is a psychic gestalt, an energy gestalt.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第81节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "81", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0050", "zh": "如果你们喜欢叫这个至高无上、绝对的心灵完形为上帝，那么，你们就不能企图从物质的角度把他具体化，因为他是你们的细胞核，比你们的呼吸与你更亲密。", "en": "If you prefer to call this supreme and absolute psychic gestalt God, then you must not attempt to objectify him in terms of material, for he is the nuclei of your cells, and more intimate than your breath.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第81节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "81", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0057", "zh": "有一个持续、不断折叠（ever-enfolding）、不断扩展的实相。我讲过的心灵完形金字塔代表你们所谓的所有开始和所有结束，而它又再扩展为新的开始和新的形式。", "en": "There is a constant, ever-enfolding and ever-expanding reality. The pyramids of psychic gestalts of which I have spoken represent in your terms all beginnings and all endings, which again expand into new beginnings and new forms.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第95节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "95", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0060", "zh": "我们将会用一节几乎完全用来处理能量完形的本质，届时你们就会明白，一方面这些金字塔能量完形的确取得统一的特质和高度的智力，但另一方面它们形成的又只是类似人类的一种上帝观而已。这个统一的完形我们可以称之为原始能量完形（primary energy gestalt），我喜欢它胜过于上帝这个词。", "en": "We shall have a session dealing almost entirely with the nature of energy gestalts, and you will see that while these pyramid energy gestalts do, on the one hand, achieve a unitary character and sublime intelligence, on the other hand they form only an approximation of humanity’s concept of a God. This unitary gestalt which we may call, and I prefer it to the word God, the primary energy gestalt.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第96节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "96", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0121", "zh": "实现或价值完成，意指发挥所有的能力和所有的潜能，肉体方面的潜能也包含在内。我提过的金字塔完形所经历过的这类经验就远比人类还多。不过它们与最小的，与你们之间最小的存在有所关联。", "en": "Fulfillment, value fulfillment, implies fulfillment of all abilities and all potentials, including quite physical potentials. The pyramid gestalts of which I have spoken have experiences far beyond those of any human being. Yet they are concerned with the least, with the existence of the least among you.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第177节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "177", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0125", "zh": "我们曾在课里讨论过一些……我所谓的心灵完形。你只看到这些智性金字塔的一部分……我们可以随时回来看。", "en": "We have discussed this to some degree in our sessions... I speak of psychic gestalts. You see but portions of these pyramids of intelligences... what we are able to see at any one time.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第203节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "203", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0128", "zh": "无论如何，基督的传奇有着伟大的心灵重要性，它有着内在的真实。这并不代表它是基于历史的事实。在很多方面来说，它比历史的事实更真实，人类自己创造了那本未被提供的。无论如何这个创造以十分真实的形式发生了，而且我说过它是一部分金字塔完形的人类内在认可。", "en": "The legend of Christ is of great psychic import however, and is intrinsically true. This does not mean it is based in historical fact. In many ways it is more true than historic fact, for man himself created that which had not been provided. The creation nevertheless happened in quite real terms, and is part of mankind’s inner recognition of the pyramid gestalts of which I have spoken.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第213节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "213", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0157", "zh": "我们没有一个人始终都有配备，为了一般的目的，可以感知每一种形式的实相。金字塔完形能够这么做，我们帮助金字塔完形展现这个技术。但是，在多数情况下，我们必须挑拣和选择。对任何意识来说，要消化的东西太多了，除了那些非常高度发展的意识以外，但是连我对它们都知之甚少。", "en": "None of us are ever equipped, for general purposes, to perceive reality in all of its forms. The pyramid gestalts can do this, and we help the pyramid gestalts perform this feat. But as a rule we must pick and choose. There is too much for any consciousness to digest except those so highly developed that even I know little of them.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第297节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "297", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0168", "zh": "史前文明的古老概念有很多更接近任何近似真相的东西。你比较喜欢想成是神的东西基本上而且最重要的是，真的像我说过的，一个无限的能量完形；或金字塔意识。它觉知它自己是，比方说，你，约瑟。它觉知它自己，就像在你看来似乎是你未来和过去的各个自己那样。", "en": "Many of the old ideas of precivilization come closer to anything near the truth. What you prefer to think of as God is basically and above all, indeed as I have said, an infinite energy gestalt: or pyramid consciousness. It is aware of itself as being, for example, you, Joseph. It is aware of itself as what seems to you as your own future and past selves.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第311节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "311", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0196", "zh": "因此，每一个自己，作为一切万有的一部分，也保留着对那个状态的记忆。正因为如此，一切万有的每一个部分、每一个最微小的意识，都被赋予了朝向生存、变化、发展与创造的推动力。一切万有作为一个原初的意识完形而渴望进一步的存在，这还不够；它的每一个部分也都必须怀有这份决心。", "en": "Each self, as a part of All That Is, therefore also retains memory of that state. It is for this reason that each portion of All That Is, each most minute consciousness, is endowed with the impetus toward survival, change, development and creativity. It is not enough that All That Is, as a primary consciousness- gestalt, desires further being, but, that every portion of it also carry this determination.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第426节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "426", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0262", "zh": "反之，在最初，再次的，是有个神圣的心理完形（gestalt）——我是指一个存在，其实相不能以“存在”（being）这个字来定义，因为它就是所有存在由之而出的那个来源。那个存在存在于一个心理的次元（长长的停顿），一个广阔的现在，在其中所有过去、现在或未来的一切东西全都保持在它的密切注意里，在一个神圣的范畴里安立不动——这范畴是在这样一个灿烂的关注里，以致最伟大和最低下的、最大和最小的，都同等的在一个多重眷爱的不变焦点里。", "en": "In the beginning there was instead, once more, a divine psychological gestalt—and by that I mean a being whose reality escapes the definition of the word “being,” since it is the source from which all being emerges. That being exists in a psychological dimension (long pause), a spacious present, in which everything that was or is or will be (in your terms) is kept in immediate attention, poised in a divine context that is characterized (long pause, eyes closed) by such a brilliant concentration that the grandest and the lowliest, the largest and the smallest, are equally held in a multiloving constant focus.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第886节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "886", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0263", "zh": "在某些基本而重要的方面，你们自己的意识是那神圣完形的一部分。就你们的尘世经验而言，把物质和意识分开是个形而上学的、科学的和创造性的错误，因为意识在物质生命中将它自己具体化为物质。", "en": "In certain basic and vital ways, your own consciousness is a portion of that divine gestalt. In the terms of your earthly experience, it is a metaphysical, a scientific, and a creative error to separate matter from consciousness, for consciousness materializes itself as matter in physical life.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第886节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "886", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0265", "zh": "你们所知的物质世界是独特的，对宇宙本身的重要性是不可或缺的，它是那个宇宙天生的一部分。然而，它也完全是它自己的实相，那实相是依赖组成它的每一种生命的感知力。那是意识的一个创造，由那神圣的存在完形升起为一个独特的表现——而那神圣的存在完形具有如此不可想象的幅度，以致它全部的实相无法出现在它自己的诸多实相、它自己的诸多世界中的任一个内。", "en": "(Pause at 9:23.) The physical world as you know it is unique, vital to the importance of the universe itself. It is an integral part of that universe, and yet it is also quite its own reality. That reality is dependent upon the perceptions of each kind of life that composes it. It is a creation of consciousness, rising into one unique kind of expression from that divine gestalt of being—and that divine gestalt of being is of such unimaginable dimensions that its entire reality cannot appear within any one of its own realities, its own worlds.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第888节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "888", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0267", "zh": "那么，在开始，CU’s——意识单位，存在于一个神圣的心理完形内，被赋予那“超越的本体”之不可想象的创造力。它们自己开始创造、探索，并完成那些使它们独具特性的天生的价值。它们以波和粒子两者运作，一部分为它们自己的创造性骚动所指挥，一部分被一切万有的不可满足的创造力所指挥，而开始了那将时间、空间和你们整个宇宙带入存在的工作。那么，它们是最先的存有。", "en": "In the beginning CU’s, then, units of consciousness, existing within a divine psychological gestalt, endowed with the unimaginable creativity of that sublime identity, began themselves to create, to explore, and to fulfill those innate values by which they were characterized. Operating both as waves and particles, directed in part by their own creative restlessness, and directed in part by the unquenchable creativity of All That Is, they embarked upon the project that brought time and space and your entire [universe] into being. They were the first entities, then.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第889节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "889", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "你身边正在发生的完形：家庭、班级和这堂课", "note": "AI总结：完形不只在天上，也发生在你家客厅。赛斯说过，如果说每个人格是一个能量完形，那么每个家庭群体也是；罗家的团结，动力其实是「对抗母亲的感觉」——整个家庭里运作着一种微妙的心理完形。他在《灵魂永生》里进一步说，家庭必须被视为心灵活动的完形，它们有一个团体里没有任何成员知觉到的主观身份；各种军事、教会、狩猎团体的成员，也常在另一生形成家属关系去解决旧问题。赛斯课本身就是活例子：珍、罗和他三人因为过去紧密的连结，形成了一个真的心灵完形；做测验时他们几乎像一个整体、一个完形来工作；珍那一端的扩展加上他那一端的扩展，形成了他所谓的完形——心理桥梁。连一堂课都可以有情感完形，ESP 班读这些资料也会凝聚出群体完形。不过赛斯澄清过界限：他不是罗和珍联合本体形成的那一个完形，那额外的能量只是帮他沟通得更完全。", "src": "第 71、158、168、176、177、222、241、348、356、395、399、550 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 71 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 158 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 168 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 176 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 177 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 222 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 241 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 348 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 356 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 395 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 399 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 550 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-048-e0043", "zh": "约瑟，在我们的沟通里，你的心灵强度极为重要；没有它，沟通就会变得万分困难；因为我们3个在过去的紧密连结，使得我们之间有可能达到一个心灵的完形。而我们确实有一个心灵完形。", "en": "Your psychic strength is extremely important, Joseph, in our communications; and without it adequate communication would be most difficult; because we three have been closely involved in the past, the psychic gestalt between us is possible. And we do have a psychic gestalt.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第71节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "71", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0100", "zh": "约瑟，在这一节有一个很重要的情感性行动；因为我们的课探讨到很多层面，我觉得遗憾的是，这一个层面在大多数时候遭到忽略。我正努力为今晚的课提供一个情感完形，它本身就是一个经验，也是一堂课。", "en": "There is an emotional action, Joseph, in this session that is important; for our sessions deal with many layers, and I regret that this one layer is at most times neglected. I am endeavoring to give this evenings session an emotional gestalt that will be an experience in itself, and in itself a lesson.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第158节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "158", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0119", "zh": "你也必须知道，成为她儿子的那个存有，也为了自己的目的，事先了解这样的环境，并且选择了它们。这里有许多角色层面的问题须纳入考量，因为如果说每个人格是一个能量完形的话，那么每个家庭群体也会是一个能量完形，这些活动和互动形成了各个家庭群的特质和本性。", "en": "You must also realize that the entity who became her son also chose the circumstances, knowing of them in advance, for his own purposes. There are many character aspects to be considered here. For if each personality is an energy gestalt, then also each family group is also an energy gestalt. The actions and interactions form its characteristics and nature.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第176节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "176", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0135", "zh": "在做我们测验的时候，我们几乎是以一个整体，就像是一个完形来工作的，而约瑟，你也是这里的一部分。我们对这最后的测验很具体，但首先必须有自由。", "en": "We work in our tests almost as one organism, as a gestalt, and you also have a part here Joseph. We were certainly specific with this last test, but there must be freedom first.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第222节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "222", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0141", "zh": "我首先会讨论我们自己的特定情况，然后再进行比较概括的讨论。你知道，有鲁柏的自我和他的潜意识。也有属于他整体人格一部分的领域或层面。在我们的例子当中，则是一个完形人格或心理桥梁。", "en": "I will first discuss our own particular circumstances, and then proceed to a more general discussion. There is Ruburt’s ego, and his subconscious, as you know. There are also other areas or levels that are part of his whole personality. In our case a gestalt personality or a psychological bridge.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第241节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "241", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0142", "zh": "同时，由于我们使用的方法，一些转译通常是必要的。在很多情况下，这种转译是通过中介心理架构来完成，这个架构只不过是最接近鲁柏的人格和我自己的人格交集的心理点，因为他身为一个人格是不会逐渐隐没的。他会在扩展中延伸自己。他那一端的心理扩展，以及我这一端的心理扩展，形成了我说过的完形，心理桥梁。", "en": "At the same time, because of the methods we use, some translation is often necessary. In many cases this translation is done by the intervening psychological framework, which is simply the psychological point closest to the meeting of Ruburts personality and my own, for he does not fade out as a personality. He extends himself in an expansion. The psychological expansion on his end, and the psychological expansion on my end, form the gestalt, the psychological bridge, of which I have spoken.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第241节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "241", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0176", "zh": "她以一种奇怪的方式将家庭凝聚在一起，纯粹是因为他们非常团结一致，以便对付她，要不是这样，他们才不会这么团结。整个家庭中，有一种相当微妙的心理完形在运作。此时他们团结的动力，其实不是在父亲身上，而是在对抗母亲的感觉上。", "en": "In a strange manner she holds the family together, simply because they unite so strongly against her. Without this they would be less united. A rather delicate psychological gestalt operates with the family as a whole. The father actually is not the uniting principle here, but the feeling against the mother, at this time.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第348节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "348", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0177", "zh": "所有这些都存在于家庭的完形之中。母亲已经建立一些行为模式，让她能够以这种方式运用攻击性，而且很有效地化解其他人的攻击性。在你的家人中，除了史蒂芬之外，没有其他人可以透过这种方式——也就是化解的方式，来处理攻击性。不过他的方式与母亲的方式不同。", "en": "All of this exists within the gestalt of the family. The mother has set up patterns of behavior that allow her to use aggressions in this way, and to dissipate the aggressions of others to a large degree. Within your family, no others save perhaps Stephen, could handle aggressions in this manner—that is, dissipate them. Although his way would be different from the mother's.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第356节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "356", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0179", "zh": "我目前在ESP班上使用的资料确实会吸引其他学生，不是因为这是我的资料，而是因为这些资料中可以感知到真理，将提供内在具有的动力，还会将学生凝聚在一起，会形成一种群体完形的运作，肯定对学生和鲁柏都很有帮助。他等了这么久才把这些资料介绍给班上学生学习，这绝非偶然。", "en": "My material, now being used in classes (ESP), will indeed draw other students. Not because it is mine but because truth can be sensed within it. It will provide a built-in impetus. It will also bind the students together as a group. There will be a group gestalt operating that should result in very definite benefits to them and to Ruburt. It is no coincidence that he waited this long to introduce the material for class study.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第395节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "395", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0183", "zh": "这与我无关，除了我们课堂中的共同努力可以帮我更完全地透过来之外。也就是说，我不是你们的联合本体（united identities）所形成的完形，然而这些额外的能量，确实有助于我与你们沟通。", "en": "This has nothing to do with me, except that working together in our sessions helps me come through more completely. That is, I am not that gestalt formed by your united identities. That additional energy does help me communicate however.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第399节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "399", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0209", "zh": "常常，各种的团体——军事团体、教会团体、狩猎团体——其中的成员会在另一生中形成家属关系，然后再以新的方式解决他们旧的问题。必须把家庭视为心灵活动的完形；家庭本身有一个主观的成份，这个团体中却没有某个成员对此点有所知觉。", "en": "Oftentimes members of various groups — military groups, church groups, hunting groups, will in another life form family relationships in which they will then work out old problems in new ways. Families must be considered as gestalts of psychic activity; they have a subjective identity, of which no particular member of the group may be aware.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第550节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "550", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0117", "zh": "鲁柏已建立起非常大的信心，我们必须慢慢进行，特别是在一开始的时候，因为如果我们的基础不够扎实，就不会有进步，整个冒险计划会失败。这些事没有所谓的命定，我们的冒险计划并没有注定要如何，我们的冒险计划代表了能量完形以相当自然的方式，聚集在一起。无论如何，我们必须以这种不用彼此冲击的方式相聚。", "en": "To a large measure Ruburts confidence has been won. It was most necessary that we go slowly, particularly in the beginning, for if our foundation was not strong we would have never progressed. The whole venture would have been lost. There is no fate in these matters. Our venture was not fated to be. Our venture represents gestalts of energy coming together in quite natural manners. It was necessary however that we meet in such a manner without clashing.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第168节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "168", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "完形会出问题吗？——人格、健康与创造", "note": "AI总结：完形视角给健康和人格整合开了一扇很实用的窗。维系一个完形的效率，靠的是各部分的合作：每个分子有自己的自我意象，潜意识有，自我也有；当行动能不受阻碍地流动，合作关系就保住了。最常见的错误出在自我——它总想否认自己对这合作的依赖，设置障碍，如果由它胡来，它会想吞掉整个有机体的其他面向。所以把整个人格整合成一个有效率的精神完形，依靠的是自由不受阻断的行动之流；理想状况是自我倾听内我，把能量向外引导，造福整个完形架构。疾病在这里有个让人松口气的定位：阻碍性行动并不是基本人格结构或行动完形的一部分，跟每个原子分子的记忆构成的惊人结构相比，它相对不重要，方法得当不难清除。创造也是完形活动：艺术家该走进风景里去感受形式底下那个整体的完形，一幅画里既有构成材料的个别意识，也有艺术家整体构思产生的完形意识——观赏者从中学到的永远是活的知识。", "src": "第 157、160、162、163、164、165、255、401、412、425、463 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 157 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 160 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 162 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 163 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 164 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 165 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 255 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 401 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 412 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 425 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 463 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-048-e0099", "zh": "在艺术创作上使用你大部分的能量，是你的本质，你必须以这种方式把它转向外界。你的本质要求你用丰富的内在资料形成新的完形，而且在为它们作画时，自动使它们向外连结。你需要内在资料和内在旅程，但这些一定要节制，不能过度。", "en": "It is in your nature to use much of your energy in artistic creation. You must then turn it outward in this manner. From the wealth of inner data your nature demands that you form new gestalts, and in painting them you automatically relate them outward. You need the inner data and the journeys inward, but these must always be of a disciplined nature, and not overdone.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第157节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "157", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0102", "zh": "这里也回想一下最小的粒子与细胞和器官之间的合作关系。各个分子有自己的自我意象，若非如此，分子就无法以物质建构的方式存在。潜意识有自己的自我意象，自我也有自己的自我意象。只要行动能流动，不受到阻碍，维系完形效率所需的合作关系就得以保持下去。最常见的错误是来自于自我，在很多情况下，自我会想办法否认自己对这种合作关系的依赖，因此形成了障碍，也形成某种程度上可以被视为恶性的反暗示，在其中，如果自我能为所欲为，就会封锁住整个有机体的所有其他面向，然后胡作非为。", "en": "Recall here also the cooperation that exists between the smallest particles and the cells and organs. Each molecule has its own self-image, without which it could not exist as a physical construction. The subconscious has its own self-image, the ego has its own self-image. When action is allowed to flow unimpeded, the cooperation that is necessary to maintain the efficiency of the gestalt is maintained. It is most frequently the error of the ego, who upon many occasions attempts to deny its dependency upon this cooperation, that sets up impediments, and sets up counter suggestions that can be somewhat considered cancerous, in that if it had its way the ego would envelop all other aspects of the whole organism, and run riot.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第160节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "160", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0104", "zh": "下列的基本主题，对于了解我们正要讨论的内容有其必要，特别是对任何实际上的应用更是如此；实体物质的建构；心理和电子完形会导致自己的形成；梦宇宙的本质；电子系统，因为它与物质宇宙和内在精神完形都相关；行动的本质；精神围场（mental enclosure）;精神基因（mental gene）；以及上述所有主题与它们的行动实相之间的关系。", "en": "The following basic subjects are necessary for an understanding of what we are trying to say, particularly for any practical application: the construction of physical matter; the psychological and electrical gestalt that results in the formation of a self; the nature of the dream universe; the electrical system, as it is related to both the physical universe and the inner psychic gestalt; the nature of action; mental enclosures; mental genes; and again, all of these subjects in relationship to their reality as action.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第162节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "162", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0106", "zh": "所以就任何人类人格而言，有一点很重要，就是要学习一些方法，让行动在人格之内，能随心所欲地依循正常的指引方向，如此一来，可避免这些无效的支流，阻碍了个体主要的指引方向和目标。 若要将整个人格整合为一个心理个体、一个有效率的精神完形，显然得依赖自由自在未受阻断的行动之流。这里的任何阻断，都可能对人格本身的完整性构成最大的威胁，因为人格的某一面向会牺牲其他面向，而从中获益。", "en": "On the part of any human personality, therefore, it is extremely important that methods be learned to let action follow its normal directive bent within the personality, therefore avoiding these abortive offshoots that impede main directives and purposes of the unit as a whole. The integration of the whole personality as a psychological unit, and as an effective psychic gestalt, is obviously dependent upon the free and unimpeded flow of action. Any impediments here can be most threatening to the integrity of the personality itself, for one aspect of the personality would benefit at the expense of other aspects.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第163节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "163", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0110", "zh": "这是一个理想状况，因为在这种情况下，自我会倾听内我的声音，然后将它的能量向外引导出来，而对整体完形架构带来助益。你们所谓的负面暗示，往往是自我所做的判断，因为这种暗示是由自我对潜意识起作用，也有可能反过来，由潜意识对自我起作用。这种由自我所做的暗示实际上是可以被捉到的，而且也能由正面或建设性的暗示取代。", "en": "This is the ideal circumstance, for when this is the case then the ego listens to the inner self, and then directs its energy outward in a way that is beneficial for the whole gestalt framework. What you call negative suggestions are often judgments of the ego, for suggestion works from the ego to the subconscious, as well as it works the other way around. Such suggestions made by the ego can indeed be caught, and positive or constructive suggestions given to replace them.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第163节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "163", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0112", "zh": "将阻碍性行动接受为自己一部分的时间越长，造成的问题会越严重。无论如何，阻碍性行动或疾病毕竟不是基本人格结构或行动完形的一部分，事实上，人格结构是由出生时就形成的行动模式所组成。每个原子与分子的记忆，所形成的结果实在是惊人的结构，对比之下，这种阻碍性行动就相对不重要，因此一旦用对方法，不难将其去除。", "en": "The longer the impeding action is accepted as a part of the self, the more serious the problem. The impeding action or illness however is not a part of the basic personality structure, or action gestalt, which is composed of action patterns formed since birth. Compared to this truly astounding structure, that is the result of the memory of every atom and molecule, this impeding action is relatively unimportant, and when correct methods are used, it can be dislodged without too much difficulty.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第164节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "164", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0113", "zh": "不过，在这种状况下，转变还是来自内在。由于活跃的人格完形真的非常复杂，组成它的行动相互交织在一起，因此只有该人格内心深处的直觉，才能比较完整了解这个人格系统的运作状况。", "en": "In such a case, however, the shifting still come from within. The active gestalt of the personality is indeed so complex, the actions that compose it are so intertwined, that only the deep, interior intuitions of the personality involved will ever come close to a complete understanding of the workings of the particular personality system.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第165节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "165", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0144", "zh": "作者提出了几个绝佳的重点，但是没有说出真正的要点。他们想像心理结构是一个完形，由自我主导，由各种需求和潜力所形成。当主导的自我基于任何原因放松它的控制或变得虚弱时，那么根据他们的观念，任何一个次要团体都可以接管。", "en": "The authors made several excellent points, without however carrying the main point in any actuality. They conceive of the psychological structure as a gestalt, dominated by the ego, formed by various needs and potentialities. When the dominating ego relaxes its control for any reason or becomes weakened, then according to their concept any one of the subsidiary groups may take over.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第255节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "255", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0185", "zh": "就象征意义上来说，身为艺术家的你，不该为了更清楚看到风景而后退，而是应该进入风景中，才能有更明确的感受。不管是什么时间，只要你去感受形式底下特殊且整体的完形，那么形式的创造就会自然真实地随之而来。", "en": "You as artist, symbolically speaking, should not step backward to see the landscape more clearly, but step into it so that you can feel it more clearly. If you sensethe peculiar and overall gestalt that is beneath the form at any given time, then creation of the form will follow naturally and truly.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第401节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "401", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0192", "zh": "这种意识是由构成画作材料的个别意识所组成，但同时也包含出艺术家整体构思所产生的完形意识。观赏者从观赏画作中学到的任何东西，永远都是活的知识，都会改变观赏者自己的本质。", "en": "The consciousness is composed of the individual consciousness that make up the material that is within the painting, and yet there is also a gestalt consciousness that is the result of the artist's overall conception. Anything that an observer learns from looking at the painting is always living knowledge, that alters his own makeup.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第412节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "412", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0194", "zh": "你们的自我由那看似对它切近过去之记忆的东西中获得安心感。一个失去了过去事件之记忆的人会感到不安而茫然，但其他种类的人格完形却以迥然不同的方式运作。取代那支配、或看似支配思想、任何心理活动与外显行动之时间顺序的，是联想的过程、分支与可能性。在某种程度上，你们可以通过检视自己意识之流而对这一点获得一些概念。但这种比较是极为表面的，因为即便在这里，延续性依然主宰一切，只不过联想得到了更大的发挥。", "en": "Your ego gains assurance from what seems to be the memory of its immediate past. A man who loses memory of past events feels insecure and lost, but other types of personality gestalts operate far differently. Instead of a time sequence that governs or seems to govern thought, mental activity of any kind, and overt action, you have associative processes, offshoots, and possibilities. To some extent you can gain an idea of this through an examination of your own stream of consciousness. But the comparison is highly superficial, for here too continuity reigns, even though associations are given greater play.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第425节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "425", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0198", "zh": "一方面，他自己的完形得到了扩展，因为自我结构包含了远多于平常的知觉。更多的行为被识别和诠释。然而，说话系统和心智官能必须经过训练才能处理额外的数据；这当然在这个过程中造成了一些扭曲。", "en": "On the one hand his own personality is enlarged in that the self structure includes far more perceptions than ordinarily. Further actions are recognized and interpreted. The speaking systems however and mental faculties have to be trained to handle the additional data; this of course causing some distortions along the way.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第463节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "463", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "意识的算术：完形越滚越大", "note": "AI总结：最后是完形在宇宙尺度上的运作方式。赛斯有一句漂亮的总结：意识的算术没有被消灭，它是乘法而非除法——当身份不断形成新的创造性努力和相关的完形，每一种组合里都记得所有其他联盟的意识。意识借着认识自己而成就自己，那知识把它改变成一个更大的完形，完形又试着认识并成就自己，以此类推；它以波和粒子两种方式运作，共同形成无穷无尽的心理完形，有些部分在时空里当「心理粒子」，有些部分在时空之外以波的方式流动。这一路滚上去：一些系统里可以由同一个内我冒出三四个「人」，前提是一个觉性组成的完形；透过内在感官，可能的自己们全都知觉到自己是那整个完形的一部分；连过去世的亲人也有一种完形式的「根源梦」用来沟通。在赛斯自己的人格完形里，早年那位妇人仍活着、怀着感激。而你们经常由其中冒出来的，正是那些真正了不起的意识完形。", "src": "第 291、398、565、589、683、725、744、890、904 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 291 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 398 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 565 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 589 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 683 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 725 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 744 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 890 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 904 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-048-e0156", "zh": "现在。有些女性会在梦中认同公牛（bull）。在梦中，很多女性有你们会称为男性反应的表现。有些男性在梦中有你们会称为女性反应的表现。公牛也可能代表做梦者认为是牛脾气（bullheaded）的人。一个斗牛的梦可能就会形成。变化是无止境的。因为前世的经验，有些通用意象具有强烈的个人意义。然而，通用意象不只渲染了梦状态。这些意象是思想据以进化的第一个基础。这几乎等同于细胞的思考过程，但它实际上是一个相互关系的完形（gestali of relatedness），细胞的理解在过去和现在都发生于此，并且传遍物质有机体。", "en": "Now. Some females will identify in the dream with the bull. In dreams many females will have what you would call male reactions. Some males in dreams will have what you would call female reactions. The bull could come also to represent a person the dreamer considers bullheaded. A bullfighting dream might be formed. The variations are endless. Some generic images will have strong personal significance because of past life experiences. The generic image does not only color the dream state, however. These images are the first basis from which thought evolved. This would almost amount to a cellular thinking process, but it is actually a gestalt of relatedness in which cellular comprehension was, and is, passed throughout the physical organism.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第291节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "291", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0181", "zh": "等到肉体死亡时，他的本体将欢乐聚集在一起。人格的进进出出，就像马赛克拼图一样，每一种效果都有意义，也都有益处。在这一世中，你就是打算来从事创造和教学，所有的创造都是教学。你的存有比父亲的存有还老。我、你和鲁柏之间连结过很多次，这个完形、这些状况，过去对我们所有人都有益。", "en": "There will be a joyous gathering together of his identity when the body dies. These are like the weaving together of mosaics, the weavings of the personality in and out, and no effect is meaningless nor without benefit. In this life you were meant to create, and teach. All creation is teaching. Your entity is older than your father's. You and Ruburt and I have been connected many times. The gestalt, the conditions, have in the past been beneficial for us all.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第398节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "398", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0213", "zh": "你曾斟酌过而没用到的概念，也可以被其他的可能自己以同样的方式拣到。自然，每一个可能的自己都认为自己才是真正的“你”，而对他们任一个而言，你也就是那一个可能的自己；但透过“内在感官”你们全都知觉到你们是这整个完形的一部分。", "en": "Ideas that you have entertained and not used may be picked up in this same manner by other probable you’s. Each of these probable selves consider themselves the real you, of course, and to any one of them you would be the probable self; but through the inner senses all of you are aware of your part in this gestalt.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第565节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "565", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0221", "zh": "以你们的话来说我后来活过较富有的生活，而在我人格的完形里，那妇人仍活在我内——举例来说，孩子活在大人之内——她把后来的境遇与先前的人生相比，而充满了感激。她促使我更善用我的优势。", "en": "In the gestalt of my personality, as in your terms I lived later richer lives, that woman was alive again in me — as, for example, the child is alive in the adult, and filled with gratitude comparing later circumstances to the earlier existences. She urged me to use my advantages better.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第589节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "589", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0236", "zh": "你把一个我—自己（I-self）当作是进化的主要而终极的结果。虽然，当然还有其他的本体有着许多这种我—自己，每一个都跟你一样的觉察而独立，而同时也觉察到它们存在于其中的那个更大的本体。意识借着认识自己而成就自己。以你们的说法，那知识把它改变成一个更大的完形，那完形于是又试着认识并成就自己，以此类推。在你们的地球上，意识曾经在一个与刚才所说不同的层面上，以人与动物两者做实验，但心里想达成那目标——举例来说，一群动物里的每一个动物都十分觉察对那群动物的共同知识，也觉察在任何一个个别领土里会遭遇的危险，以及一个心理结果，在其中，这群动物的集体意识认知到每个动物的个别意识，并且保护它。", "en": "You think of one I-self (spelled) as the primary and ultimate end of evolution. Yet there are, of course, other identities with many such I-selves, each as aware and independent as your own, while also being aware of the existence of a greater identity in which they have their being. Consciousness fulfills itself by knowing itself. The knowledge changes it, in your terms, into a greater gestalt that then tries to fulfill and know itself, and so forth. There have been experiments upon your earth (by consciousness) with both men and animals at a different level than just mentioned, but with that in mind — herds of animals, for example, with each animal quite aware of the joint knowledge of the herd, the dangers to be encountered in any individual territory, and a psychological structure in which the mass consciousness of the herd recognized the individual consciousness of each animal, and protected it.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第683节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "683", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0238", "zh": "在某些具体存在的系统里，一个多重人之建立是由同样的内我里冒出三或四个“人”，每个把他自己的那些特性都利用到极致，不过，这必须以一种“觉性所组成之完形”为前提，在其中，每一个都知道并且能参与其他那些个的活动：此处你有一个集体意识之不同版本。你有没有看出这之间的关联？", "en": "In some systems of physical existence, a multipersonhood is established in which three or four “persons” emerge from the same inner self, each one utilizing to the best of its abilities those characteristics of its own. This presupposes a gestalt of awareness, however, in which each knows of the activities of the others, and participates; and you have a different version of mass consciousness. Do you see the correlation?", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第683节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "683", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0240", "zh": "所有的意识，在其所有的形式里，都同时存在。这很难解释而不至于显得像是自我矛盾。回到我们的球茎与花。以基本的说法，它们同时存在。不过，以你们的说法，就好像那未来之花由它的“未来”向回叫那球茎，而告诉它如何去造那朵花。记忆在时间里向后及向前运作，那朵花——向回叫那球茎，怂恿它“向前”，而提醒它它（可能的未来）的发展——以你们的话来说，是像一个未来的自己或一个更为进步的自己，它有了答案，而的确可以相当实际的被依赖。神明们可以以同样的方式被看待，不过，是在一个更大的尺度上：而且在那个范畴里被了解的话，它们可以被依赖。当你们被陷在对人性之有限概念里时，去把神明个人化几乎是一种自然的倾向。对人性之更大观念的确会引你对真正了不起的意识完形——你经常由其中冒出来——略有几瞥。", "en": "All consciousness, in all of its forms, exists at once. It is difficult, without appearing to contradict myself, to explain. Go back to our bulb and flower. In basic terms they exist at once. In your terms, however, it is as if the flower-to-be, from its “future” calls back to the bulb and tells it how to make the flower. Memory operates backward and forward in time. The flower — calling back to the bulb, urging it “ahead” and reminding it of its (probable future) development — is like a future self in your terms, or a more highly advanced self, who has the answers and can indeed be quite practically relied upon. The gods can be seen in the same light, only on a larger scale; and understood in that context, they can be relied upon. It is almost a natural tendency to personify the gods while you are caught up in limited ideas of personhood. Larger concepts of personhood will indeed lead you to some glimpse of the truly remarkable gestalts of consciousness from which you constantly emerge.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第683节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "683", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0247", "zh": "生物上存在着的经常互换意味着那组成一个男人或一个女人的同样物质材料可以被分散，而稍后形成一只蟾蜍，一只海星，一条狗或一朵花，它可以被分布到数不清的不同形式里。那意识的算术并没有被消灭，它是乘法而非除法。当身份继续形成新的创造性努力，以及相关的完形时，在每个形式里的回忆是所有其它的组合，所有其它的联盟的意识。没有歧视，没有偏见。", "en": "The constant interchange that exists biologically means that the same physical stuff that composes a man or a woman may be dispersed, and later form a toad, a starfish, a dog or a flower. It may be distributed into numberless different forms. That arithmetic11 of consciousness is not annihilated. It is multiplied and not divided. Reminiscent within each form is the consciousness of all the other combinations, all of the other alliances, as identity continually forms new creative endeavors and gestalts of relatedness. There is no discrimination, no prejudice.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第725节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "725", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0249", "zh": "且说上个礼拜，当鲁柏谈到那些是如此的“做梦专家”之土人时，你问：“但为什么他们没有更进步呢？”然而，我知道你了解到，以你们的说法，除非你们在其它方向有进展，否则你们自己作为一个文明的进步会嘎然而止。这是你们的文明正在学习的：你们不能强暴你们的地球；生命的起源并不是因为，在存在之庞大可能性里有一些孤立的（物质）遇见另一个（相似的物质）、再另一个，又再另一个、直到一串分子可以破造成，而“自己”被形成了。用这个比喻，意识也不存在为被广大距离分开的简单有机体，却是存在为一个复杂的完形。", "en": "(To a student:) Now last week, when Ruburt [Jane] was speaking about the natives who are such expert dreamers, you asked: “But why are they not more progressive?” Yet I know you realize that your own progress as a civilization will, in your terms, come to a halt unless you advance in other directions. This is what your civilization is learning that you cannot rape your planet, that life did not begin as some isolated [substance] that in the great probabilities of existence met another [similar substance], and another, and then another, until a chain of molecules could be made and selves formed. Using an analogy, neither does consciousness exist as simple organisms separated by vast distances, but as a complicated gestalt.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0254", "zh": "（“意识形成身份的模式。意识移动得比光速还快，它们可以同时在不只一个地方。（见第七〇二节的注三）。意识本身作为身份或作为‘心理粒子’，它们可以以一种无拘无束的方式运作。意识也可以以波状方式运作，而流过其它的这种粒子。意识可以共同形成无穷无尽的组合，形成心理的完形，然后，这些完形之某些部分可以在时空里运作为‘心理粒子’，同时其它部分则在时空之外以波状方式运作。这些代表族类之无意识成分，而在物质存在里它们则变得‘粒子化’了。”", "en": "“Consciousness forms patterns of identities. They move faster than the speed of light. They can be in more than one place at one time. (See notes 5 and 6 for Session 702.) They can operate in a freewheeling fashion as identities in themselves, or as ‘psychological particles.’ They can also operate in a wavelike fashion, flowing through other such particles. They can form together into endless, infinite combinations, forming psychological gestalts. Certain portions of these gestalts can then operate as ‘psychological particles’ in time and space, while other portions operate in a wavelike manner outside of time and space. These represent the unconscious elements of the species, which become ‘particleized’ in physical existence.” Although these final paragraphs from the 775th session contain many ideas, I want to stress two of them that I find especially evocative: Seth’s reference to many reincarnations in one accepted lifetime, and the unconscious elements of the species being represented by its wavelike characteristics.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0269", "zh": "意识单位把它们自己变成EE单位，以一个你可称之为环形的方式，而非线形的方式，而在同一个过程里形成环境及其所有居民。当然，以那种说法，有其它形形色色的意识的具体显现，不只是一个行星及其居民，却是一整个有知觉的意识的完形。以那种说法，实体取向的意识的每一部分，由其特有的观点来看实相与经验，其它一切似乎都绕着它转，虽然这可能涉及一个比你们自己的场较小或较大的一般性场。", "en": "Units of consciousness (CU’s), transforming themselves into EE units, formed the environment and all of its inhabitants in the same process, in what you might call a circular manner rather than a serial one. And in those terms, of course, there are only various physical manifestations of consciousness, not a planet and its inhabitants, but an entire gestalt of awareized consciousness. In those terms (underlined), each portion of physically oriented consciousness sees reality and experience from its own privileged viewpoint, about which it seems all else revolves, even though this may involve a larger generalized field than your own, or a smaller one.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第890节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "890", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-048-e0271", "zh": "在所有物种之间的差异是由这种组织引起的，所以，选择的区域被清晰的画出，而自由活动的区域也被清晰的界定。所以，可能行动的整个完形已然多少聚焦于物种的分化里。可是，在可能活动的广大结构里，更多的分化仍是必要的，而这就透过转世存在的内在通道被提供出来。", "en": "The differences among all species are caused by this kind of organization, so that areas of choice are clearly drawn, and areas of free activity clearly specified. The entire gestalt of probable actions, therefore, is already focused to some degree in the species’ differentiations. In the vast structure of probable activity, however, far more differentiation was still necessary, and this is provided for through the inner passageways of reincarnational existence.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第904节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "904", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [{"id": "q-concept-048-e0123", "zh": "（第54节中，赛斯详细解释了存有的建构。他说不能太早给我们这部分的讯息，因为我们会直接下结论说他就是鲁柏[珍]的潜意识心；而这并非如此。存有就像万事万物一样，时时刻刻都在变化。摘录赛斯的一段话：“鲁柏现在不是我自己，在他的这一世；然而他是我曾经所是的那个赛斯的一个延伸和物质化……就个人特有的一组价值完成而言，他成长、进化也扩展了……他现在是一个真实的完形，一个赛斯可以长成的可能人格之一，我代表另一个，我是另一个。”", "en": "（In the 54th session Seth went into considerable detail in explaining the construction of entities. He could not give us this information earlier, he said, because we would have leaped to the conclusion that he was Ruburt’s [Janes] subconscious mind; this is not so. As everything else does, entities constantly change. To quote Seth: “Ruburt is not myself now, in his present life; he is nevertheless an extension and materialization of the Seth that I was at one time... He grew, evolved and expanded in terms of a particular, personal set of value fulfillments... He is now an actual gestalt, a personality that was one of the probable personalities into which Seth could grow. I represent another, I am another. ”", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第183节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "183", "only_en": false}], "books": [{"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 12}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 8}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 6}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 6}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 5}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 4}, {"name": "未知的实相卷一", "count": 4}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 4}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 3}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 2}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1979], "stats": {"blocks": 6, "quotes": 76, "reading": 1, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 1}};
